<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schönberg (Mecklenburg)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Schönberg is a small town in north-western Mecklenburg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>. It was a residence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratzeburg">Ratzeburg</a> and, after the secularisation of the bishopric in 1648, the seat of government of the Principality of Ratzeburg, a detached part of Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strelitz">Strelitz</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schonberg-mecklenburg.jpg" alt="Schönberg (Mecklenburg)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kresspahl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OberteichSch%C3%B6nberg04.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
